<%# The knowledge layer's preview frame, for e2e/knowledge_transcript.spec.js.

    One render BY NAME and nothing else: the engine's own preview template,
    which writes the <turbo-frame> and renders the player, the cues and their
    styles. The controller set up its three instance variables as
    Studio::KnowledgeDocsController#preview does. Anything hand-written here
    would be the lab grading itself.

    The spacer below gives the PAGE somewhere to scroll to, as the real page
    has (the triage form sits under the preview). Without it a spec could not
    tell following that scrolls the cue list from following that scrolls the
    page: there would be no page scroll to observe. %>
<main class="p-8">
  <%= render template: "studio/knowledge_docs/preview" %>
  <div data-test="spacer" style="height: 150vh"></div>
</main>
